Article 13

In order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children from acts of violence, the family:  a. protects women and children from various violations of rights in the household;
b. encourages the formation of a harmonious, educative, independent and fully responsible family; andc. serves as a place for initial counseling and mediation for every family member suspected of violations of the rights of women and children.

Article 8

1. In efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence, the City Government is obliged to:a. guarantee the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations; b. establish and implement policy programs and activities for the protection of the rights of women and children; c. facilitate the formation of community organizations concerned with women and children;
d. cooperate with the community and/or community organizations and the private sector in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. carry out rehabilitation and empowerment of women and children who are victims of acts of violence; f. provide special protection to women and children victims of various acts of violence; andg. take preventive action in order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children. (2) The responsibility in efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.
3. Further provisions regarding the obligations of the City Government as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 14

( 1) The implementation of handling women and children victims of acts of violence includes:
a. handling complaints from victims of violence;
b. health services; andc. law enforcement and legal assistance.
2. The implementation of handling women and children victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph ( 1) is carried out through integrated services.
3. Integrated services as referred to in paragraph (2) for women and children victims of acts of violence are carried out with the principles of:a. responsive;
b. non-discriminatory;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
1. sensitive to the background and condition of victims; J. using language that is appropriate and understood by victims;
k. fast and simple;
1. empathetic;
m. fulfillment of the rights of women and children; andn. legal certainty.

Article 4

The scope of regulation of protection of women and children from acts of violence includes:
a. forms of acts of violence;'b. rights and obligations;

protection of women and children;
c. prote_d. guidance and supervision; ande. funding.

Article 11

( 1) In order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children, the City Government:
a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of community units, community leaders, religious leaders, community organizations and mass media;
b. provides guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children;
c. develops an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women and children;
d. strengthens the function of community organizations engaged in the protection and advocacy of women and children; ande. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
2. The responsibility of the City Government in efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph ( 1) is carried out by regional apparatus for women and children in accordance with their duties and functions.
3. Further provisions regarding the planning of prevention of violations of the rights of women and children are integrated by the City Government into regional development planning.

Article 17

( 1) Health services in handling women and children victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 14 paragraph (1) letter b for women and children victims of acts of violence are carried out comprehensively, accessible 24 hours, of quality and carried out with maximum health service standards.

2. Women and children victims of acts of violence have the right to health services, including:a. medical services;
b. medico-legal services; andc. psychosocial counseling.
3. Medical services as referred to in paragraph (2) letter a, are in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics.
4. Medico-legal services as referred to in paragraph (2) letter b, are a form of medical services for the purposes of evidence in the legal field.
5. Services .....

12 - (2) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. counseling services;
b. provision of safe houses;
c. spiritual guidance; andd. economic recovery.
3. The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (2), is organized by:a. UPT PPA is tasked with carrying out operational technical activities in its working area in providing services for women and children victims of acts of violence, discrimination, special protection, and other problems;
b. the position of UPT PPA is under and responsible to the Head of the Agency that administers government affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection at the city level; andc. religious institutions.

MAYOR OF PALEMBANG,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to obtain protection and guarantee of their human rights, and has the right to receive fair treatment to obtain equal opportunities and benefits in achieving life welfare;
b. that laws and regulations governing the protection of women and children in regulating efforts for women and children to be free from acts of violence in the region require regulations that can guarantee their implementation;
c. that all forms of acts of violence against citizens, especially women and children, constitute a form of violation of human rights, therefore the state, government, society, and family have the obligation and responsibility for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

In View of

